"describe the Wi-Fi link, not your measured internet speed."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2855
msgid "Compare another device or service"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2855
msgid ""
"Try another device on the same Wi-Fi and another app or website. If several "
"devices have trouble, check the router or ask your internet provider. If "
"only this computer is affected, check its adapter and Ubuntu updates."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2856
msgid "Look for nearby channel overlap"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2856
msgid ""
"The WiFi Analyzer recommendation on the Network and hardware page can help "
"you review nearby signal levels and channel use. It opens an external "
"project page after confirmation; ask the network owner before changing "
"router settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2857
msgid "Keep private details out of support requests"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2857
msgid ""
"Share the adapter model, hardware ID and driver if you need help. Do not "
"share the Wi-Fi password or private network details."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2859
msgid "Wi-Fi is connected but the internet does not work"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2860
msgid "Check whether the problem affects other devices"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2860
msgid ""
"Try another device on the same network and try a different website or app. "
"If several devices are affected, check the router or contact the internet "
"provider."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2861
msgid "Look for a network sign-in page"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2861
msgid ""
"Public Wi-Fi in places such as hotels, libraries and airports may require a "
"sign-in page, sometimes called a captive portal. Open a browser and follow "
"the network's instructions only if you expected this page. Do not ignore "
"certificate warnings or enter sensitive account details on an unfamiliar "
"page."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2862
msgid "Check the VPN if you use one"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2862
msgid ""
"A VPN or managed work or school policy can affect internet access. Check its "
"status and ask your administrator for help; do not bypass your "
"organization's VPN or security policy."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2863
msgid "Run the optional connection checks"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2863
msgid ""
"On the Network and hardware page, you can choose Test DNS and gateway or "
"Test internet connection. Each test asks first and shows its duration. DNS "
"uses your configured resolver, gateway ping stays on the local network, and "
"the internet test contacts ubuntu.com."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2864
msgid "Review network settings"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2864
msgid ""
"Open Network Settings and check that the expected Wi-Fi or wired connection "
"is active. Avoid changing proxy, DNS or manual IP settings unless your "
"network administrator or provider gives you the correct values."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2868
msgid "Use Mouse Keys"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2869
msgid "Open Pointing and Clicking"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2869
msgid "In Accessibility Settings, open the Pointing and Clicking section."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2870
msgid "Turn on Mouse Keys"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2870
msgid ""
"Mouse Keys lets you control the pointer with the numeric keypad. Turn Num "
"Lock off to use the keypad for pointer movement."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2871
msgid "Test it and turn it off if needed"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2871
msgid ""
"Try moving the pointer and clicking a simple target. Return to Pointing and "
"Clicking to turn Mouse Keys off when you are finished."
msgstr ""

#: data/se.nylander.UbuntuStart.desktop:3
msgid "Get started with Ubuntu and troubleshoot devices"
msgstr ""
